-- The artifact scrolls, all of them.
--
-- An earlier pass concluded we held complete scroll sets for four artifacts
-- out of fifty-seven. That was wrong, and wrong in a way worth writing down:
-- the search was for items with "scroll" in the name. Most artifact scroll
-- sets are not called scrolls. They are letters, journals, diaries, pages,
-- tablets, pieces, volumes and parchments -- Alvarus' Letter, Bellona's Diary,
-- Loukas' Journal, Mariasha's Wall, Staff of God Parchment. Searching instead
-- for the shape they all share, "N of 3", finds fifty-seven complete sets and
-- a hundred and seventy-one scrolls. Every artifact we have is covered.
--
-- Split across the two binders, alternating through the alphabet so each holds
-- a spread rather than one end of it, and each carries whole sets: you never
-- need both merchants to finish one artifact.
--
-- Priced flat at 300 bounty points. The templates carried their old gold
-- prices, from 30 to 19,636, which as a bounty cost would have meant one
-- scroll for a season's work and another for nothing. 300 puts a full
-- three-scroll set at 900, alongside Aphaestia's artifact credits at 289 to
-- 1,210 and below Demyphon's Master Level credits at 1,500 to 5,000.

